# Store every text file with LF line endings whatever the committing machine uses.
# Commit d30921e4 stored a CRLF copy of one file and turned a 167-line change into 12,000.
* text=auto

# A catalog (.cat) hashes the exact bytes of every file it covers. The
# BthPS3 and BthPS3PSM INFs arrive signed from upstream, and two of them mix
# line endings: BthPS3.inf has one bare LF at line 67 and
# BthPS3_PDO_NULL_Device.inf has one at line 53. Converting them in either
# direction changes those bytes and the catalog then rejects the INF, so git
# stores and checks them out untouched. ds3_winusb.inf is signed on the
# machine that installs it, so it keeps the CRLF checkout.
PadForge.App/Resources/**/*.inf text eol=crlf
PadForge.App/Resources/BthPS3/BthPS3/*.inf -text
PadForge.App/Resources/BthPS3/BthPS3PSM/*.inf -text

# A shell script checked out with CRLF does not run: bash reads the carriage
# return as part of each command. Pin LF whatever core.autocrlf says.
*.sh text eol=lf
